{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 471678, "name": "K K", "username": "chomskynoam", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-01-12T21:10:18.677Z", "cooked": "<p>I am experiencing Bluetooth stuttering when playing audio over video, the web, local MP3s, etc. This only happens with Bluetooth — not with wired headphones or any other audio output. Bluetooth audio cuts out to silence, then plays perfectly for about 5 seconds, cuts out again, and repeats. I have seen this both with AirPods and with a Bluetooth desk speaker.</p>\n<p>I first experienced this on Fedora 42, I think after an update. After switching back to the Fedora 43 Live CD, the issue was gone there. So I reinstalled Fedora 43, and the issue was fixed — but only until updating again.</p>\n<p>This time, I enabled etckeeper and kept track of installed packages. One of the packages that differs between the Fedora 43 Live CD and the current upstream system must be the culprit. I selectively downgraded Bluetooth, BlueZ, and kernel packages, but without success.</p>\n<p>Do you have any hints for me? Is this a known or already tracked bug? I see a spike in Bluetooth-related bugs recently.</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-01-12T22:07:24.002Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 685, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 3434.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179413, "topic_slug": "bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update", "display_username": "K K", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/fedora-43-workstation-bluetooth-headphones-connection-cutting-out-after-a-recent-update/178715/2", "internal": true, "reflection": true, "title": "[Fedora 43 Workstation] Bluetooth Headphones Connection Cutting Out After A Recent Update", "clicks": 24}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 1}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 31605, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update/179413/1", "event": null, "calendar_details": [], "reactions": [{"id": "bluethumb", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 1, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 474265, "name": "deanrock", "username": "deanrock", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-01-25T19:51:04.617Z", "cooked": "<p>Hey, I’ve been experiencing the same issue on two computers.</p>\n<p>This started happening after upgrading <code>plasma-workspace</code> (and dependencies) from <code>6.4.5-4.fc43</code> to <code>6.5.5-1.fc43</code>.</p>\n<p>I’ve tracked it down to the upgrade of <code>kdeconnectd</code> from <code>25.08.2-1.fc43</code> to <code>25.12.1-1.fc43</code>.</p>\n<p>Temporary solution that seems to work is to remove KDE Connect:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\"># dnf remove kde-connect\nPackage                                                                              Arch             Version                                                                              Repository                                                 Size\nRemoving:\n kde-connect                                                                         x86_64           25.12.1-1.fc43                                                                       &lt;unknown&gt;                                               4.2 MiB\nRemoving unused dependencies:\n fuse-sshfs                                                                          x86_64           3.7.5-1.fc43                                                                         &lt;unknown&gt;                                             125.4 KiB\n kde-connect-libs                                                                    x86_64           25.12.1-1.fc43                                                                       &lt;unknown&gt;                                               2.4 MiB\n kdeconnectd                                                                         x86_64           25.12.1-1.fc43                                                                       &lt;unknown&gt;                                              67.5 KiB\n kf6-kpeople                                                                         x86_64           6.22.0-1.fc43                                                                        &lt;unknown&gt;                                             671.2 KiB\n libfakekey                                                                          x86_64           0.3-25.fc43                                                                          d15e557246b143e68b4d7cf7c8078e9c                       45.5 KiB\n openssh-askpass                                                                     x86_64           10.0p1-6.fc43                                                                        &lt;unknown&gt;                                              19.7 KiB\n qt6-qtconnectivity                                                                  x86_64           6.10.1-1.fc43                                                                        &lt;unknown&gt;                                               1.5 MiB\n\nTransaction Summary:\n Removing:           8 packages\n\nAfter this operation, 9 MiB will be freed (install 0 B, remove 9 MiB).\nIs this ok [y/N]: \n</code></pre>\n<p>After logging out and logging back in, stutters were gone.</p>", "post_number": 2, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-01-25T19:51:04.617Z", "reply_count": 2, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 145, "reads": 27, "readers_count": 26, "score": 765.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179413, "topic_slug": "bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update", "display_username": "deanrock", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://discussion.fedoraproject.org/t/fedora-43-workstation-bluetooth-headphones-connection-cutting-out-after-a-recent-update/178715/4", "internal": true, "reflection": true, "title": "[Fedora 43 Workstation] Bluetooth Headphones Connection Cutting Out After A Recent Update", "clicks": 1}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [{"id": 2, "count": 2}], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 31848, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update/179413/2", "event": null, "reactions": [{"id": "heart", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}, {"id": "party", "type": "emoji", "count": 1}], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 2, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": true, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 474307, "name": "K K", "username": "chomskynoam", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-01-26T07:07:48.261Z", "cooked": "<p>Looks good! I removed <code>kde-connect</code> just like you said, restarted and my Bluetooth is now stutter free again.</p>\n<p>These are the packages that I removed:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-plaintext\">    Package changes:\n    -0:fuse-sshfs-3.7.5-1.fc43.x86_64\n    -0:kde-connect-25.12.1-1.fc43.x86_64\n    -0:kde-connect-libs-25.12.1-1.fc43.x86_64\n    -0:kdeconnectd-25.12.1-1.fc43.x86_64\n    -0:kf6-kpeople-6.22.0-1.fc43.x86_64\n    -0:libfakekey-0.3-25.fc43.x86_64\n    -0:openssh-askpass-10.0p1-6.fc43.x86_64\n</code></pre>\n<p>I will report back if it stays this way.</p>\n<p>Edit: I think the issue is solved now. Playing Bluetooth audio for 2h straight without any issues. This is most likely the matching bug report: <a href=\"https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=513536\">https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=513536</a></p>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-01-26T09:27:27.786Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 13, "reads": 24, "readers_count": 23, "score": 74.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179413, "topic_slug": "bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update", "display_username": "K K", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 2, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=513536", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "clicks": 67}], "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 31848, "username": "deanrock", "name": "deanrock", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 31605, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update/179413/3", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 474702, "name": "Moritz", "username": "morak", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/morak/{size}/43605_2.png", "created_at": "2026-01-28T10:53:41.609Z", "cooked": "<p>Holy shit dude, this worked. Wtf is wrong with KDE Connect?!</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-01-28T10:53:41.609Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 2, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 1, "reads": 18, "readers_count": 17, "score": 8.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179413, "topic_slug": "bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update", "display_username": "Moritz", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 31848, "username": "deanrock", "name": "deanrock", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/aad0ee/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 25448, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update/179413/4", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 474705, "name": "Moritz", "username": "morak", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/morak/{size}/43605_2.png", "created_at": "2026-01-28T10:54:41.403Z", "cooked": "<p>Could you update me when this isseu has been resolved?</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-01-28T10:54:41.403Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 3, "reads": 18, "readers_count": 17, "score": 23.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179413, "topic_slug": "bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update", "display_username": "Moritz", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "", "reply_to_user": {"id": 31605, "username": "chomskynoam", "name": "K K", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 25448, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update/179413/5", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 474706, "name": "K K", "username": "chomskynoam", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/c/38bc3b/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-01-28T11:03:10.738Z", "cooked": "<p>You better watch the KDE bug report directly</p>", "post_number": 6, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-01-28T11:03:10.738Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 5, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 11, "reads": 17, "readers_count": 16, "score": 58.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179413, "topic_slug": "bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update", "display_username": "K K", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 25448, "username": "morak", "name": "Moritz", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discussion.fedoraproject.org/morak/{size}/43605_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 31605, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update/179413/6", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 482081, "name": "anon _", "username": "series692", "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/s/51a2da/{size}.png", "created_at": "2026-03-03T19:04:43.737Z", "cooked": "<p>Has anyone noticed what I can best describe as high-pitched faint digital noise from their headphones’ right channel after using this fix? I don’t have this issue on other devices. Tried switching to the different available codecs to no avail. Sounds like a communication signal aliasing into the audible range? It only appears during and for a few seconds after playback.</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 7, "updated_at": "2026-03-03T19:05:32.322Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 10, "reads": 12, "readers_count": 11, "score": 52.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 179413, "topic_slug": "bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update", "display_username": "anon _", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 32498, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 0, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": true, "wiki": false, "mentioned_users": [], "post_url": "/t/bluetooth-stutters-since-update-reproducible-after-dnf-update/179413/7", "event": null, "reactions": [], "current_user_reaction": null, "reaction_users_count": 0, "current_user_used_main_reaction": false, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}], "stream": [471678, 474265, 474307, 474702, 474705, 474706, 482081]}, "timeline_lookup": [[1, 295], [2, 282], [4, 280], [7, 246]], "suggested_topics": [], "tags": [{"id": 800, "name": "bluetooth", "slug": "bluetooth"}, {"id": 342, "name": "problem", "slug": "problem"}], "tags_des